        {
          "post_id": "495339",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following context-free grammars:</p><p>$$<br>\\begin{aligned}<br>& G_1: S \\rightarrow A|B, A \\rightarrow a A| a, B \\rightarrow b B \\mid b \\\\<br>& G_2: S \\rightarrow A B, A \\rightarrow a A|a, B \\rightarrow b B| b<br>\\end{aligned}<br>$$</p><p><br>Which one of the following pairs of languages is generated by $G_1$ and $G_2$, respectively?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\left\\{a^m \\mid m&gt;0\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{b^n \\mid n&gt;0\\right\\}$ AND $\\left\\{a^m b^n \\mid m&gt;0, n&gt;0\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\left\\{a^m b^n \\mid m&gt;0\\right.$ OR $\\left.n&gt;0\\right\\}$ AND $\\left\\{a^m b^n \\mid m&gt;0, n&gt;0\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\left\\{a^m \\mid m&gt;0\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{b^n \\mid n&gt;0\\right\\}$ AND $\\left\\{a^m b^n \\mid m \\geq 0, n&gt;0\\right\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\left\\{a^m \\mid m \\geq 0\\right\\} \\cup\\left\\{b^n \\mid n \\geq 0\\right\\}$ AND $\\left\\{a^m b^n \\mid m \\geq 0, n \\geq 0\\right\\}$</li></ol>",
